---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Fair Housing";
const description = "HOUSE OF KATHY IS COMMITTED TO FAIR HOUSING.";
const permalink = `${Astro.site?.href}fairHousing`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  permalink={permalink}
  current="fairHousing"
>
  <div class="SOP">
    <h1>Standard Operating Procedure for Buyers of Real Estate</h1>

    <p>
      At <strong>House of Kathy</strong>, one of our four core values is <strong
        >"Ethics."</strong
      > In the interest of transparency, we have standardized our operating procedures
      for working with real estate clients.
    </p>

    <h2>IDENTIFICATION</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>House of Kathy</strong> does not have a company policy requiring its
      Sales Agents, Associate Brokers, or any member of staff to obtain identification
      or proof of U.S. citizenship from Buyers or Sellers prior to showing property
      or entering into an agreement to purchase or list property.
    </p>

    <p>
      When identification is required for a specific transaction, service,
      offer, contract, lender requirement, or other legitimate business purpose,
      the applicable documentation may be requested.
    </p>

    <h2>PREQUALIFICATION AND PROOF OF INCOME</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>House of Kathy</strong> does not have a company-wide policy requiring
      its Sales Agents or Associate Brokers to obtain a mortgage pre-qualification,
      mortgage pre-approval, proof of funds, or proof of income from every prospective
      Buyer prior to showing a property available for sale.
    </p>

    <p>
      However, prospective purchasers may be asked to provide documentation
      demonstrating their financial ability to purchase a property when
      reasonably required by a Seller, lender, property-specific requirement,
      transaction requirement, or other legitimate business purpose.
    </p>

    <p>Such documentation may include, but is not limited to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Mortgage pre-qualification or pre-approval;</li>
      <li>Proof of available funds;</li>
      <li>Bank or financial account statements;</li>
      <li>Pay stubs or other employment income documentation;</li>
      <li>Tax returns or other documentation of self-employment income;</li>
      <li>Documentation of other lawful income or financial resources; or</li>
      <li>
        Other reasonable documentation requested for the purpose of establishing
        the prospective Buyer's ability to complete the proposed transaction.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Any request for proof of income or financial qualification must be applied
      consistently and for a legitimate business purpose. <strong
        >House of Kathy</strong
      > and its associated licensees shall not discriminate against a prospective
      Buyer based upon a lawful source of income. Lawful sources of income must be
      evaluated consistently and without discrimination.
    </p>

    <p>
      It should be noted that Sellers of real property may establish reasonable
      financial qualification requirements or request evidence that a
      prospective Buyer has the financial ability to complete a purchase. A
      lender may also require financial documentation as part of the mortgage
      approval process.
    </p>

    <p>
      Prospective purchasers are encouraged to contact a lender prior to
      enlisting the services of a licensed real estate agent so that they are in
      the strongest position to present an offer acceptable to a Seller should
      they identify a property for which they would like to present an offer.
    </p>

    <h2>EXCLUSIVE BUYER CONTRACTS</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>House of Kathy</strong> does not require that a prospective Buyer of
      Real Estate enter into an Exclusive Right to Represent Buyer contract prior
      to showing a property available for sale.
    </p>

    <p>
      As independent contractors, Sales Agents and Associate Brokers may explain
      the benefits of working under such an agreement and, as such, we provide
      them with a contract should they choose to present it to their customers
      for their consideration.
    </p>

    <h2>NEW YORK STATE REQUIRED DISCLOSURES</h2>

    <p>
      New York State Law requires real estate licensees who are acting as agents
      of Buyers or Sellers of property to advise the potential Buyers or Sellers
      with whom they work of the nature of their agency relationship and the
      rights and obligations it creates.
    </p>

    <p>
      As such, it is also the policy of <strong>House of Kathy</strong> that all licensees
      present all Buyers, Sellers, Landlords, and Tenants with the <strong
        >NEW YORK STATE DISCLOSURE FORM</strong
      >, furnished by the Department of State, <strong
        >FOR BUYER AND SELLER</strong
      > and/or <strong>LANDLORD AND TENANT</strong>, upon first substantive
      contact.
    </p>

    <p>
      Pursuant to New York State Law, all licensees associated with <strong
        >House of Kathy</strong
      > are required to provide to a prospective purchaser, tenant, seller, or landlord,
      upon first substantive contact, a disclosure notice furnished by the Department
      of State containing substantive provisions of the New York State Human Rights
      Law.
    </p>

    <p>
      This notice may be provided by email, text, electronic messaging system,
      facsimile, or hard copy. An electronic communication containing a link to
      the required disclosure notice shall be permissible, provided the
      communication also contains text informing the prospective purchaser,
      tenant, seller, or landlord that the link contains information regarding
      the New York State Human Rights Law.
    </p>

    <p>
      Oral disclosure does not satisfy the requirements of either the Law or of <strong
        >House of Kathy</strong
      >.
    </p>

